     The availability of both explore mode and wizard mode are conditional,
based on definitions in the config files at the time NetHack is compiled.
By default, they're both enabled, but the wizard name is port-specific.
The wizard name for VMS can be found in [.include]vmsconf.h; to change it,
edit that file and then rebuild.

     To switch to explore mode while in a regular game, use the 'X' command.
What that buys you is an opportunity to be restored to full hit points and
keep playing whenever your character gets killed.  In exchange for that,
your score won't be recorded.

     To start a game in explore mode, specify -x or -X on the command line.
In addition to the life-saving mentioned above, you'll receive a fully
charged wand of wishing in your initial inventory.  It's for experimenting;
real players want to see their characters on the high score list.  ;-)

     To start a game in wizard (aka debug) mode, you must be logged in to
the account that's compiled into nethack.exe, and also specify "-D" on the
command line.  That one is case sensitive and the quotes are required.
(Instructions for the other ports vary considerably; I'm referring to the
VMS port here.)  If you try to use wizard mode from the wrong username, or
if the program was built without wizard mode, you'll end up in explore mode
instead.  Wizard mode is for debugging, not for getting unlimited wishes...
(and it has nothing whatever to do with playing as a wizard character).

